WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.129
Continuous monitoring helps organizations maintain awareness of changing security posture,

00:00:04.129 --> 00:00:07.351
system state, threats, vulnerabilities, control effectiveness, and risk.

00:00:07.351 --> 00:00:12.991
It is the practice of watching the things that matter after launch, after authorization,

00:00:12.991 --> 00:00:15.811
after deployment, and after the last assessment.

00:00:15.811 --> 00:00:19.034
Systems change, threats change, and business use changes.

00:00:19.034 --> 00:00:24.271
Monitoring helps teams see those changes while there is still time to respond.

00:00:24.271 --> 00:00:27.494
Effective monitoring is scoped, risk-based, evidence-driven, owned, reviewed,

00:00:27.494 --> 00:00:29.106
and connected to remediation.

00:00:29.106 --> 00:00:33.134
It should cover assets, identities, configurations, vulnerabilities, logs, changes, alerts,

00:00:33.134 --> 00:00:37.969
incidents, and controls in a way that matches risk and business context.

00:00:37.969 --> 00:00:41.997
The program should prioritize critical systems, sensitive data, privileged access,

00:00:41.997 --> 00:00:44.817
exposed services, known weaknesses, and mission-important workflows.

00:00:44.817 --> 00:00:48.443
Strong monitoring depends on telemetry quality and operational discipline.

00:00:48.443 --> 00:00:50.054
Logs must be reliable.

00:00:50.054 --> 00:00:52.471
Evidence must be current and traceable.

00:00:52.471 --> 00:00:54.083
Alerts must be triaged.

00:00:54.083 --> 00:00:55.694
Findings must have owners.

00:00:55.694 --> 00:00:57.306
Exceptions must be documented.

00:00:57.306 --> 00:00:58.917
Reports must support decisions.

00:00:58.917 --> 00:01:01.334
Control evidence must reflect real operations.

00:01:01.334 --> 00:01:02.543
Without those habits,

00:01:02.543 --> 00:01:08.183
monitoring can become a noisy data collection exercise rather than a risk management capability.

00:01:08.183 --> 00:01:11.003
The goal is not collecting more data.

00:01:11.003 --> 00:01:16.240
The goal is making better security and risk decisions faster and more consistently.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:21.477
Continuous monitoring should help teams understand what changed, what matters, who owns it,

00:01:21.477 --> 00:01:25.506
what action is needed, and how the program should improve.

00:01:25.506 --> 00:01:30.340
That is what turns monitoring from passive observation into practical security operations.
